/// Timing-aware partition of captured values around owned mutations.
///
/// Values on paths never mutated in the capture are external seed candidates.
/// An analyzer directory observed before a later action mutates one of its
/// direct children is an explicit bootstrap candidate rather than an immutable
/// external listing. Analyzer observations after the first captured child
/// mutation are generated namespace state and are withheld from replay inputs.
/// Values observed by their mutating owner before its first mutation candidate
/// are also bootstrap candidates. Values at or after that candidate are
/// withheld from replay inputs until effect semantics prove their provenance.
/// Other cross-owner mutation observations remain unsupported. This sanitized
/// seal is diagnostic and grants no snapshot admission or replay authority.
